          }
        ],
        "author": {
          "name": "Oleg Drokin",
          "email": "green@whamcloud.com",
          "date": "2026-10-30 19:49:56.000000000",
          "tz": -240
        },
        "committer": {
          "name": "Oleg Drokin",
          "email": "green@whamcloud.com",
          "date": "2026-11-02 19:53:39.000000000",
          "tz": -300
        },
        "subject": "LU-20984 obdclass: check Netlink request fits in the message",
        "message": "LU-20984 obdclass: check Netlink request fits in the message\n\nThe lustre Netlink family's start and command handlers walk the\nnested attributes of a request using the length stored in its\nfirst attribute header, which was never compared with the length\nof the message received, so a malformed request could make the\nparser read past the end of the message.\n\nCheck the first attribute with nla_ok() against the message length\nbefore walking it.\n\nTest-Parameters: trivial\nFixes: 86ba46c24430 (\"LU-9680 obdclass: user netlink to collect devices information\")\nFixes: 3c9ab551b322 (\"LU-11850 obd: support target_obd using Netlink\")\nFixes: 5803284ac3a5 (\"LU-11850 obd: use netlink to get lustre stats\")\nSigned-off-by: Oleg Drokin <green@whamcloud.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:Opus-5 llm_code_and_review_tools\nChange-Id: I9e8ec62f46e7881bb5492effc651390b06586568\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
